arade Accommodation                            12.3  \\n\",","       \"              Food and beverage services               -2.1  \\n\",","       \"              Transport services                      -10.6  \\n\",","       \"Züri Fäscht   Accommodation                             8.2  \\n\",","       \"              Food and beverage services               -0.3  \\n\",","       \"              Transport services                        3.4  \"","      ]","     },","     \"execution_count\": 15,","     \"metadata\": {},","     \"output_type\": \"execute_result\"","    }","   ],","   \"source\": [","    \"variants = {\\n\",","    \"    \\\"Without days 25-31 (%)\\\": calculate_baselines(exclude_month_end=True),\\n\",","    \"    \\\"Only ±14 days (%)\\\": calculate_baselines(max_distance=14),\\n\",","    \"}\\n\",","    \"sensitivity = event_results.groupby([\\\"event_name\\\", \\\"merchant_category\\\"])[[\\\"percentage_deviation\\\"]].mean()\\n\",","    \"sensitivity.columns = [\\\"Main baseline, ±28 days (%)\\\"]\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"for label, variant in variants.items():\\n\",","    \"    check = event_results[[\\\"event_id\\\", \\\"merchant_category\\\", \\\"date\\\", \\\"event_name\\\", \\\"scaled_value\\\"]].merge(\\n\",","    \"        variant, on=[\\\"event_id\\\", \\\"merchant_category\\\", \\\"date\\\"], validate=\\\"one_to_one\\\")\\n\",","    \"    assert (check[\\\"n_controls\\\"] >= MIN_CONTROLS).all(), f\\\"{label}: too few controls on an event day\\\"\\n\",","    \"    check[\\\"deviation\\\"] = 100 * (check[\\\"scaled_value\\\"] - check[\\\"baseline\\\"]) / check[\\\"baseline\\\"]\\n\",","    \"    sensitivity[label] = check.groupby([\\\"event_name\\\", \\\"merchant_category\\\"])[\\\"deviation\\\"].mean()\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"sensitivity.round(1)\"","   ]","  },","  {","   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",","   \"id\": \"afc5a817\",","   \"metadata\": {},","   \"source\": [","    \"## 8. Interpretation and limitations\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"### Interpretation\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"All numbers come from the figures, the heatmap and the tables above. For each category we separate **what we observe**, **possible explanations** (not verified) and what the analysis **cannot** show.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"**Accommodation**\\n\",","    \"* *Observed:* above the baseline on the event days of all seven editions:\\n\",","    \"  * Street Parade: +1.6% (2019) to +16.1% (2024),\\n\",","    \"  * Züri Fäscht: +15.1% (2019) and +5.7% (2023).\\n\",","    \"* In five editions the event-day deviation is higher than that of 80–93% of the non-event days in the same ±28-day window; in Street Parade 2019 and Züri Fäscht 2023 the share is 61–63%. These shares are calculated from the daily deviations and are not shown as a separate table.\\n\",","    \"* The event-type means stay positive in both sensitivity variants (+8.2% to +12.3%). The day after Street Parade (Sunday) is also above the baseline in all five editions (+6% to +16%).\\n\",","    \"* *Possible explanations:* more or longer hotel stays, or higher prices on event weekends. The data contain neither guest numbers nor prices, so higher accommodation *spending* does not necessarily mean more overnight visitors.\\n\",","    \"* *Conclusion:* the editions show a consistent positive deviation, but the data cannot show that the events caused it.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"**Food and beverage services**\\n\",","    \"* *Observed:* below the baseline on Street Parade day in all five editions (−3.8% to −15.4%, mean −10.2%). The editions differ: in 2019, 2024 and 2025 the event day is among the lowest days of its window, in 2022 and 2023 it is in the middle. For Züri Fäscht the two editions point in opposite directions (−3.9% and +10.5%).\\n\",","    \"* *Sensitivity:* with the ±14-day baseline, the Street Parade mean changes from −10.2% to −2.1%. The result therefore depends strongly on which comparison days are used, and the size of any event-day deviation is uncertain.\\n\",","    \"* The marked 1 August values are far below the baseline in every Street Parade window (−22% to −46%). They coincide with the public holiday and are not Street Parade effects. Other possible explanations for weak days before Street Parade, such as seasonal patterns, are not tested here; no school-holiday calendar was used.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"**Transport services**\\n\",","    \"* *Observed:* slightly below the baseline on Street Parade day in all five editions (−4.1% to −10.9%). For Züri Fäscht the editions disagree (−2.9% and +12.4%).\\n\",","    \"* *Sensitivity:* the Street Parade mean ranges from −2.3% to −10.6% across the baseline variants, so no robust conclusion is possible.\\n\",","    \"* The large negative values on 1 August (−44% to −64%) coincide with the public holiday and are not Street Parade effects.\\n\",","    \"* The series has an unexplained structural break around January 25, 2021, whose cause has not been confirmed. Comparisons across years should be interpreted cautiously.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"**Street Parade vs. Züri Fäscht**\\n\",","    \"* For both events, Accommodation spending was above the baseline on the event days.\\n\",","    \"* For the other categories the five Street Parade editions mostly share the same sign, while the two Züri Fäscht editions disagree.\\n\",","    \"* With two editions, differences between the events cannot be assessed reliably.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"**Do the event days stand out from the surrounding days?**\\n\",","    \"* Mostly not. All six event-day averages lie inside the 5th–95th percentile range of the non-event days.\\n\",","    \"* Even within ±14 days, the line charts show deviations of ±20–60% on other days, e.g. the marked 1 August dips and high Transport values late in the month. Patterns also differ between editions, and other events (marked or not) may influence individual days.\\n\",","    \"* Accommodation is the only category where the event days are mostly in the upper part of each edition's window.\"","   ]","  },","  {","   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",","   \"id\": \"3fd0940c\",","   \"metadata\": {},","   \"source\": [","    \"### Limitations\\n\",","    \"* **No proof of causality.** These are observational comparisons with nearby days. Weather, tourism or other events on the same day can also influence spending.\\n\",","    \"* **Comparisons between years.** COVID-19 and other economic changes affected spending levels between 2019 and 2025. Each baseline comes from the same window, so these changes mainly affect comparisons between editions, not the baselines themselves.\\n\",","    \"* **Transport break.** Transport services shows a substantial structural break around January 25, 2021, whose cause has not been confirmed. All windows lie within one year, so the baselines are not affected, but comparisons of Transport across years should be interpreted cautiously.\\n\",","    \"* **Baseline quality.** Only 1 August and Whit Monday are excluded; this is not a complete public-holiday calendar. School holidays are not excluded, because no verified calendar was available. Other events, including the marked ones, remain in the control dates. Late-month patterns can also affect the baseline, and the results partly depend on the baseline window (see section 7).\\n\",","    \"* **Züri Fäscht.** With only two editions, conclusions about Züri Fäscht are especially tentative.\\n\",","    \"* **Scaled card spending.** The data are scaled card payments at points of sale. They exclude cash, e-commerce and other economic activity, and are not CHF amounts.\\n\",","    \"* **Attendance.** One-day (Street Parade) and three-day (Züri Fäscht) attendance figures are not comparable, so attendance is not used as a numerical predictor.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"### Conclusion\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"In these card data, spending on the event days of Street Parade and Züri Fäscht does not differ much from similar nearby days.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"The most consistent observation concerns Accommodation:\\n\",","    \"* spending was above the baseline on the event days of all seven editions;\\n\",","    \"* on average +9.8% for Street Parade (five single-day editions) and +10.4% for Züri Fäscht (two editions, each averaged over its three festival days);\\n\",","    \"* the event-type means stay positive in both sensitivity variants.\\n\",","    \"\\n\",","    \"This describes the observed editions; it does not establish that the events caused the higher spending. Deviations in Food and beverage services and Transport services are small compared with the day-to-day variation, differ between editions and depend on the baseline definition.\"","   ]","  },","  {","   \"cell_type\": \"code\",","   \"execution_count\": 16,","   \"id\": \"a7705b6a\",","   \"metadata\": {","    \"execution\": {","     \"iopub.execute_input\": \"2026-11-01T16:44:20.725849Z\",","     \"iopub.status.busy\": \"2026-11-01T16:44:20.724769Z\",","     \"iopub.status.idle\": \"2026-11-01T16:44:20.733881Z\",","     \"shell.execute_reply\": \"2026-11-01T16:44:20.732572Z\"","    }","   },","   \"outputs\": [","    {","     \"name\": \"stdout\",","     \"output_type\": \"stream\",","     \"text\": [","      \"Exported: ['q1_street_parade_combined.pdf', 'q1_street_parade_combined.png', 'q1_zueri_faescht_combined.pdf', 'q1_zueri_faescht_combined.png', 'q1_event_heatmap.png']\\n\"","     ]","    }","   ],","   \"source\": [","    \"for name in [\\\"q1_street_parade_combined\\\", \\\"q1_zueri_faescht_combined\\\"]:\\n\",","    \"    for suffix in [\\\".png\\\", \\\".pdf\\\"]:\\n\",","    \"        assert (FIGURE_DIR / (name + suffix)).exists(), f\\\"missing export: {name + suffix}\\\"\\n\",","    \"print(\\\"Exported:\\\", sorted(p.name for p in FIGURE_DIR.glob(\\\"q1_*_combined.*\\\")) + [\\\"q1_event_heatmap.png\\\"])\"","   ]","  }"," ],"," \"metadata\": {","  \"kernelspec\": {","   \"display_name\